<Project>

  <!--
    The built-in convention packs' items, imported at the top of Sdk.props:
    before Microsoft.NET.Sdk, and so before Directory.Build.props.

    `Update` changes only items that already exist, and does nothing, without
    a warning, when there are none yet. Declared here, the pivots exist when
    a repository's Directory.Build.props and then the project body are
    evaluated, so an `Update` in either applies, in the order of precedence:
    the SDK's default, then the repository's, then the module's own.
    Microsoft.NET.Sdk declares its default Compile items after
    Directory.Build.props, so a repository-wide `<Compile Update>` there does
    nothing. That is tolerable for Compile, whose metadata never leaves the
    project. A module's pivot metadata ends up in its manifest, and a common
    module's manifest is shared by every module that references it.

    Directory.Build.targets would see the items too, but it is imported after
    the project body, so the repository would override the module.

    Only items can come this early:
      - A property default here would run before Directory.Build.props, so a
        default the repository sets with a "'$(X)' == ''" condition would
        never apply, and a property derived from another would capture its
        empty value. Property defaults stay in
        FluentMigrator.Net.Sdk.Conventions.props.
      - Item conditions and includes are evaluated after every property, so
        they see the final values of $(EnableDefaultSourceModelItems) and
        $(FlywayLocationRoot) wherever those are set.
      - Custom packs from $(CustomSourceModelConventionPacks) can't move here:
        the list is set in Directory.Build.props, which hasn't been read yet.
  -->
  <Import Project="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)conventions/*.props" />

</Project>
